// @hash 3db67464afc6
{
  // The push policy of a task a person drives: push only when asked. Sent with the Send agent to update action of the updates row; the Mandate itself adds no line for it. It is filled with no variable.
  "pushOnRequest": "Push only when the user asks you to, with `./equin push -m \"…\"` — never on your own initiative.",
  // The push policy Never: the agent stops at a ready branch and raises a flag. It is filled with no variable.
  "pushNever": "Do NOT push. When the build is `ok`, stop and raise a flag so a person reviews the branch — say what changed and why.",
  // The push policy If uncontroversial: the agent pushes only a small, local change with no decision left to make. It is filled with no variable.
  "pushSafe": "Push with `./equin push -m \"…\"` ONLY if the change is uncontroversial: small and local, no behaviour or API a person relies on changes, no design choice is left to make, and every check passes. **You are authorized to push such a change without asking.** Anything else: do NOT push — raise a flag that says what needs a decision.",
  // The push policy When checks pass: the agent pushes once every check passes. It is filled with no variable.
  "pushChecks": "**You are authorized to push this task's change without asking** once every check passes and the build is `ok`: `./equin push -m \"…\"`.",
  // The line a push policy other than on request becomes in the agent's Mandate section. Filled at each use: {{policy}} (the push policy's own prompt).
  "mandatePushLine": "Pushing: {{policy}}",
  // When the agent closes its conversation with exit_clean, for a task a person reviews in the open conversation. Told after an outcome report is saved; the Mandate itself adds no line for it. It is filled with no variable.
  "exitOnRequest": "When the user asks you to wrap up, you may close this conversation with `exit_clean` once your work landed and there is nothing they need to know. Never call it on your own: the conversation stays open for review.",
  // When a supervisor's worker closes its own conversation with exit_clean: in its Mandate section, and after its outcome report is saved. It is filled with no variable.
  "exitWhenDone": "Close this conversation with `exit_clean` on your own — without waiting to be asked — but only once the whole session is finished: your change pushed and the push landed (or, when your push policy keeps you from pushing, your flag raised), your outcome report submitted when your mandate requires one, no build, push, test or other `./equin` op still running, and nothing left to do. Submitting the report is not the end: if a push is still to run or in flight, finish it first (`./equin await <op>` until it settles) and only then close. Whoever supervises you can still message you: that resumes you."
}
